From 04d03250f271e9ad8403167f00b07b8e025a1902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:30:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hooks): make enforcement hooks respect disabled config
 (refs eda6d866)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The self-contained enforcement hooks (.forge/hooks/check-tdd.js and
forge-native-hook.js) enforced with ZERO reference to .forge/config.yaml, so a
disabled gate/rail still fired — progressive/configure-anytime setup was
dishonest.

RED: added tests proving a disabled TDD rail (workflow.gates['rail.tdd_intent']
or top-level rails.tdd_intent) and an empty protectedPaths list still enforced.
GREEN: both hooks now read config at run time and no-op when their governing
primitive is disabled — TDD gate inert when rail.tdd_intent disabled;
protected-path inert when protectedPaths resolves empty. Missing/unparseable
config FAILS TOWARD enforcement so no gate is silently dropped. yaml lib is used
when present, with a conservative raw-text fallback for truly standalone hooks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
